WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.140
What's a must-have superpower for&nbsp;
an undersea, water-breathing king?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:08.591
The power to fly through the air with&nbsp;
teeny tiny wings on his feet, of course!

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.900
Namor's mutant power of flight is one&nbsp;
of his most recognized comics abilities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:18.780
and it appears his MCU debut will put it on full&nbsp;
display, complete with those trademark wings on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:23.820
his ankles. Throughout the new trailer for "Black&nbsp;
Panther: Wakanda Forever," we see instances where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:28.620
Namor is either levitating or flying around&nbsp;
in combat. The question of whether his wings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:33.120
are a part of his flying power is a point of&nbsp;
debate in the comics. Some fans believe the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:37.860
wings simply help him steer and maneuver, while&nbsp;
some other source of power, possibly telekinesis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:42.720
is thought to lift him. The fact that he is seen&nbsp;
levitating would point toward this being the case.

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:47.700
An interesting thing to note about Namor's&nbsp;
flight: Namor was most likely the first superhero&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:52.680
to ever fly in a comic book, with his flying&nbsp;
powers predating those of Shazam and Superman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:57.240
the latter of whom originally just made giant&nbsp;
leaps as opposed to soaring through the skies.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:00.795
With that in mind, it's only fitting&nbsp;
that Namor will get to exercise those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.795 --> 00:01:05.769
ankle wings on his cinematic debut. However,&nbsp;
this is only the beginning of his powerset.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:09.840
While flying around is cool and all,&nbsp;
it's going to take someone with both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:14.160
speed and strength to compete with Marvel's&nbsp;
Black Panther, no matter who may be donning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:18.360
the famous moniker following T'Challa's&nbsp;
tragic death. As we've seen in comics and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:22.380
"Wakanda Forever" clips, Namor is more&nbsp;
than competent in both of these arenas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:26.640
possessing raw abilities that allow him&nbsp;
to stand toe-to-toe with even the Hulk.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:29.460
"That can't be good."

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:34.620
Namor is a powerhouse when it comes to durability&nbsp;
and super-strength, and these abilities increase&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:39.960
exponentially when he is in the water, meaning&nbsp;
that even if one finds Namor tough to beat on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:44.940
the surface, a quick dip in the ocean will make&nbsp;
him even tougher. While Namor's primary mutant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:50.220
power is generally considered flight, it's his&nbsp;
strength, endurance, and unrelenting stubbornness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:54.660
that will make him seem unstoppable even to&nbsp;
the forces of Wakanda. Though his water-fueled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:59.640
strength is quite similar to another ocean-loving&nbsp;
superhero from the DC Universe, it's worth noting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:04.864
that Namor is actually the original aquatic&nbsp;
superhero, predating Aquaman by two years.

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:09.960
Out of all the abilities that Namor has in&nbsp;
the comics, it's his telepathic abilities and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:15.000
intelligence that prove most commanding. If Namor&nbsp;
weren't powerful enough on his own, his ability to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:19.440
command sea life and the Talocans, with nothing&nbsp;
but his mind might be his most imposing power.

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:24.900
But can Namor speak to fish? The answer is&nbsp;
complicated. While he does have a telepathic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:28.800
connection with sea life, it's more of an&nbsp;
influence over them that allows him to get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:33.300
creatures to do what he wants them to do. This&nbsp;
is as opposed to the way that Aquaman generally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:37.680
"communicates" with sea life in a more verbal&nbsp;
manner. For instance, those whales swimming in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:42.540
the "Wakanda Forever" clips alongside the people&nbsp;
of Talocan? Namor is basically mind-controlling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:47.136
them into joining the fight. Which is something&nbsp;
he can also do with other elements of the ocean.

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:51.420
Namor has the ability to manipulate&nbsp;
water and the weather around him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:56.220
in a similar way to Storm of the X-Men. We see&nbsp;
brief scenes of this power in action during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.220 --> 00:03:00.720
the "Wakanda Forever" trailer where the Talocan&nbsp;
leader appears to have flooded Wakanda itself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:05.460
It's a moment reminiscent of the comics,&nbsp;
where Namor did just that. This wasn't the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:10.860
first time Namor attacked a human city in such&nbsp;
a manner, either, as 1941's "Human Torch" issue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:16.200
5 saw him flood New York City to devastating&nbsp;
effect, an event that still lives in infamy.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:20.280
Believe it or not, Namor was the first&nbsp;
"entity" to ever successfully invade&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:24.060
Wakanda in the comics, though he was&nbsp;
defeated by T'Challa and the Avengers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:27.540
and things eventually got sorted&nbsp;
out between everyone. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:31.740
when it comes to Marvel's Cinematic Universe,&nbsp;
we will have to wait and see if Wakanda and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:35.595
Talocan will ever make amends because&nbsp;
this is a pretty devastating attack.

